# What this repo does NOT track.
#
# The data is the point here, so nothing that matches a data file is listed:
# every .csv under data/ and design/, the generated review .md files and
# technology-database-template.xlsx are all deliberately tracked, because a
# reviewer needs to see what a pipeline run changed. What is listed below is
# only what a tool writes for its own benefit and can regenerate from scratch.

# Python bytecode and tool caches. Every script here is run straight from the
# working tree (python database/harmonized/populate.py), so these appear on any run
# and are pure noise in a diff.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Environments. Nothing in the pipeline depends on where the interpreter lives.
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# marimo's scratch directory, written beside a notebook when one is run.
__marimo__/

# Excel and Word lock files: an open workbook leaves ~$name.xlsx beside it, and
# committing one records a file that exists only while the app is open.
~$*
*.tmp

# OS metadata.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Primary documents. The source PDFs, workbooks and saved web pages stay on
# disk beside their extractions but are not tracked: git holds only what was
# extracted from them (the CSVs and their _meta/_nodes sidecars) and the
# manifest that says where each document came from (source-details_*.csv).
database/raw-data/**/*.pdf
database/raw-data/**/*.doc
database/raw-data/**/*.docx
database/raw-data/**/*.xls
database/raw-data/**/*.xlsx
database/raw-data/**/*.xlsm
database/raw-data/**/*.xlsb
database/raw-data/**/*.ods
database/raw-data/**/*.html
database/raw-data/**/*.mhtml
cims/reporting-accounting/context/*.xlsx
# the retired manifest workbook is the project's own file, not a source document
!database/raw-data/superseded/source_details.xlsx
# intake working folders (triage lists, mapping proposals, page renders, and
# duplicate copies), archived 2026-10-30 after the intake rounds finished
archive/intake/high/
archive/intake/medium/
archive/intake/low/
# bulk source datasets kept beside their extractions (primary data, like the PDFs)
database/raw-data/gov-usa/nrel/nrel_2025_annual-technology-baseline-electricity-data.csv
database/raw-data/superseded/nrel_2024_annual-technology-baseline-electricity-data.csv
database/raw-data/background-no-data-extracted/epa_2023_methane-mitigation-options.json
database/raw-data/background-no-data-extracted/epa_2023_methane-mitigation-emission-join.json
database/raw-data/**/*.zip
database/raw-data/iea/iea_2026_methane-tracker-*-data.csv
database/raw-data/other-reports/iai/iai_2026_*-data.csv
database/raw-data/**/*.json
database/raw-data/iea/iea_2026_methane-abatement-model-*-data.csv
database/raw-data/iea/iea_2026_methane-abatement-model-notes.txt

# Large extracts of the EIA bulk files: regenerate with
# database/raw-data/gov-usa/eia/prices/eia_bulk_extract.py from the (ignored) zips.
database/raw-data/gov-usa/eia/prices/eia_2026_bulk-seds_prices.csv
database/raw-data/gov-usa/eia/prices/eia_2026_bulk-elec_prices.csv

# Petrinex facility-year metrics (bulk, ~26 MB): regenerate with
# database/raw-data/gov-can/petrinex/petrinex_annual.py then petrinex_summary.py from the (ignored) zips.
database/raw-data/gov-can/petrinex/petrinex_2026_facility-metrics_ab-sk.csv

# files the Claude app saves into the connected folder
Claude outputs/
